[{:db/id "q-8720/selection/d49d489b8643593ea6da23ce0954b46f7709c930833e7da7a68231c37da9ea83" :answer/id #uuid "a3464676-c759-5e6c-b2fa-887a7e2a9bac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8720/selection/b6827fdc1097d70d880de3946592c6feac3dbe411b38a73e545d1d8a254855f0" :answer/id #uuid "20167ebf-c31f-5ccd-8d2c-3682f252954e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8720/selection/e5e20467f4ad53d124c2d4ce12a980864e847586bf9b48db9ef00ae35515cbaf" :answer/id #uuid "7cec39a0-69f0-524e-830a-c99d3badc0ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8720/selection/c64533ef977f2485d9c3a74b87efa14f38e1771b769d9b155ac1bcb25835cec2" :answer/id #uuid "97e341fc-f53d-5bfc-bd3a-23ade7428705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8720/selection/5a18a04037db8fb54981765a28c8873b72588e95b96bcbd8c9e26cdf5f75f179" :answer/id #uuid "30e715b7-82d3-5959-9197-8f18a36ad843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8720/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "176b0e2e-8b22-54dd-afac-d234aba9e08f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8720/selection/d49d489b8643593ea6da23ce0954b46f7709c930833e7da7a68231c37da9ea83" :answer-field/choices ["q-8720/selection/d49d489b8643593ea6da23ce0954b46f7709c930833e7da7a68231c37da9ea83" "q-8720/selection/b6827fdc1097d70d880de3946592c6feac3dbe411b38a73e545d1d8a254855f0" "q-8720/selection/e5e20467f4ad53d124c2d4ce12a980864e847586bf9b48db9ef00ae35515cbaf" "q-8720/selection/c64533ef977f2485d9c3a74b87efa14f38e1771b769d9b155ac1bcb25835cec2" "q-8720/selection/5a18a04037db8fb54981765a28c8873b72588e95b96bcbd8c9e26cdf5f75f179"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8720" :question/id #uuid "417331c2-762c-5bf7-9ba6-a204c035e2e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-8720" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-\\pi +{x}_{1}=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824/selection/7b8e96ce4b79877556d736620d780e9a943f61f3051914969cc7d2ede3f8be3b" :answer/id #uuid "85239dd0-8edd-577c-be8d-3ad4a247bfda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824/selection/8d08c752f36e6235434c23715b4c6ea1769cf535e935f1b5c3606027ea4b9255" :answer/id #uuid "daa3bbb7-7a62-5f02-a7c0-0b9268fa6df3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824/selection/cdd1e5d65d54e3f97cd9dc4db9127794dff119222947034a54a2b01a4df2ab37" :answer/id #uuid "561aca6a-b656-5ddc-bdc5-5fb329ac7b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer/id #uuid "4849510a-f2db-5905-a715-d49ffc472fc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824/selection/50e4889e67b91d9c30d86f1e14e03ad1f8b5d7049a71f947d8aa5fa3adc3c70b" :answer/id #uuid "6dbe7c01-e369-57d3-b4d3-2aa7b3f424bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b4d9ab4-51c5-5dc6-a7af-e60ea74a4d13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72824/selection/7b8e96ce4b79877556d736620d780e9a943f61f3051914969cc7d2ede3f8be3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-72824/selection/7b8e96ce4b79877556d736620d780e9a943f61f3051914969cc7d2ede3f8be3b" "q-72824/selection/8d08c752f36e6235434c23715b4c6ea1769cf535e935f1b5c3606027ea4b9255" "q-72824/selection/cdd1e5d65d54e3f97cd9dc4db9127794dff119222947034a54a2b01a4df2ab37" "q-72824/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" "q-72824/selection/50e4889e67b91d9c30d86f1e14e03ad1f8b5d7049a71f947d8aa5fa3adc3c70b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72824" :question/id #uuid "63edf08b-7802-5b9f-940f-83ad72d838db" :question/math-academy-id "q-72824" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-8$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-8)=-1.446\\,4…≈-1.446\\,4.\n$$\n\nSince $-1.446\\,4$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi -1.446\\,4≈1.695\\,2, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi -1.446\\,4≈4.836\\,8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.695\\,2\\cdot 4.836\\,8≈8.2\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72824/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542/selection/fb062ca592ca54d47ac3219efc1dcc598f09d92894ed2aa558c1c7bf06e25bd5" :answer/id #uuid "6d57f986-db13-514b-ab92-c979718aa86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542/selection/3826cb6859afc17fc29beb5847fa2ea888053c16a97c5e0ca18d51a86cfb06ca" :answer/id #uuid "49bce2c0-7111-5786-8d41-c1887b6cb48d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542/selection/b0042a44e98c8cf50b336ee74275344644b30297d07c83a0f30c8adefb394da2" :answer/id #uuid "e69e16d0-fee5-54d3-a02b-cc2ee311af9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8\\pi }{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542/selection/28420441481517359a953269476eab72b5407e6c08575a9703d60f0a494468c5" :answer/id #uuid "64665c65-a217-51f5-8b50-4ce3d6c2bc6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542/selection/e610ac583c710f4736f4d5544343b2233f961de9a650f480b19d3fd5b6ffe2ac" :answer/id #uuid "fc9eb9a0-3d07-5668-ac3e-e9d02100b319" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47929783-18a2-5a5a-918b-3a7c899616ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121542/selection/fb062ca592ca54d47ac3219efc1dcc598f09d92894ed2aa558c1c7bf06e25bd5" :answer-field/choices ["q-121542/selection/fb062ca592ca54d47ac3219efc1dcc598f09d92894ed2aa558c1c7bf06e25bd5" "q-121542/selection/3826cb6859afc17fc29beb5847fa2ea888053c16a97c5e0ca18d51a86cfb06ca" "q-121542/selection/b0042a44e98c8cf50b336ee74275344644b30297d07c83a0f30c8adefb394da2" "q-121542/selection/28420441481517359a953269476eab72b5407e6c08575a9703d60f0a494468c5" "q-121542/selection/e610ac583c710f4736f4d5544343b2233f961de9a650f480b19d3fd5b6ffe2ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121542" :question/id #uuid "40f7d319-bfe9-5828-b013-a9a68e7eb115" :question/math-academy-id "q-121542" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977868/assets/56726fc8331106df9b20aed561a2ed3b93fe12d90da85a8d1b92e610b19033f7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\sqrt{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $  to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121542/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121542"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274852/field-1/e52b829daa8bd68fe53c085738a0d4fbb4032f675657f14b3e43001213161d96" :answer/id #uuid "bfdf1082-baca-55f0-b3c8-148cd49f2361" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274852/field-1/1dee3a8b4e2e69484264522b7c3f6207b09ecde7ad469649dd240ad6a8e6346d" :answer/id #uuid "94f8b14f-8fe0-527f-b3be-dfaee31315b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274852/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e829784-352e-546b-b589-dc5d8deeeb5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274852/field-1/e52b829daa8bd68fe53c085738a0d4fbb4032f675657f14b3e43001213161d96" :answer-field/choices ["q-274852/field-1/e52b829daa8bd68fe53c085738a0d4fbb4032f675657f14b3e43001213161d96" "q-274852/field-1/1dee3a8b4e2e69484264522b7c3f6207b09ecde7ad469649dd240ad6a8e6346d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274852" :question/id #uuid "d180bdf2-fe1c-5547-a6bb-3dbae8427806" :question/math-academy-id "q-274852" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977868/assets/047f02622fc176fee8c6cb0e81a0434ee208648dca14102b1d96e37b901d51f2.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x+(-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274852/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274852"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321622/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "95d4ea44-d1c7-5a57-8c4b-c552f9b48ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321622/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "86ac4f73-8253-5b38-8431-20e467ca1ad5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321622/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-321622/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321622/field-2/ce38165bbdbead56ddc746e2c26cef4b23956481241cf8d8f08b8446ec20e57e" :answer/id #uuid "32b9adcf-ccbb-577c-b00a-654888926547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "189" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321622/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4104241c-1ccd-5359-ad5b-f7628f4def96" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321622/field-2/ce38165bbdbead56ddc746e2c26cef4b23956481241cf8d8f08b8446ec20e57e" :answer-field/choices ["q-321622/field-2/ce38165bbdbead56ddc746e2c26cef4b23956481241cf8d8f08b8446ec20e57e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321622" :question/id #uuid "64dbab80-af43-59e4-8d97-d949c8f2ff4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-321622" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{6}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ Round your answers to **the nearest integer**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{6})=9.4623{…}^{∘}≈{9}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${9}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={9}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+9.4623{…}^{∘}≈{189}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={9}^{∘}$ and $x={189}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321622/field-1" "q-321622/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
